e</text><line x1="154" y1="172" x2="191" y2="172" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="219" y1="172" x2="250" y2="172" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="191" cy="172" r="2.6" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="219" cy="172" r="2.6" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="191" y1="172" x2="217" y2="160" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154" y1="248" x2="250" y2="248" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250" y1="172" x2="250" y2="198" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250" y1="222" x2="250" y2="248" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="250" cy="210" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M243,210 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'An aluminium ring rests around a vertical iron core above a coil wound on the core. The coil is connected to a supply through a switch, which is open.'),
('3dca3c07-9511-5c45-96d8-3e95f5ad45b2', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 15, 15, 'An e.m.f. of 0.45 V is induced in a loop of resistance 1.5 Ω. Calculate the induced current.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.3', 'A', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'I = E/R = 0.45 ÷ 1.5 = 0.30 A. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: I = E/R. A1: I = 0.30 A.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('ea0caf6a-5e25-545c-b684-264f3521a4f3', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 16, 16, 'What is meant by an eddy current in a piece of metal?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Induced currents that circulate inside a solid conductor when the flux through it changes', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'They flow in loops within the bulk of the metal and oppose the change. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (Induced currents that circulate inside a solid conductor when the flux through it changes).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('a0ff2528-4dd3-54db-9a50-db822bf5def8', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 17, 17, 'A moving rod has an e.m.f. of 0.60 V and carries a current of 1.5 A. Calculate the electrical power produced.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.9', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = EI = 0.60 × 1.5 = 0.90 W. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: P = EI. A1: P = 0.90 W.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('d7d9f764-dc29-5006-b8dc-047baa23fe0a', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 18, 18, 'Why must the induced current oppose the change that causes it?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Otherwise energy would be created from nothing, breaking the principle of conservation of energy', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A current that helped the change would speed up the motion without any work being done. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (Otherwise energy would be created from nothing, breaking the principle of conservation of energy).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('c7136467-97a5-57f1-add4-0e3f2fdbcbfd', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 19, 19, 'A resistor dissipates 0.90 W of induced power. How much energy is transferred in 10 s?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = Pt = 0.90 × 10 = 9.0 J. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: E = 9.0 J.', 1, NULL, NULL),
('200b548d-7820-5720-90ef-558bd62bfaa1', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 20, 20, 'A solid copper plate swings as a pendulum between the poles of a magnet and stops quickly. A plate with slots cut in it swings for much longer. Why?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The slots break up the paths of the eddy currents, so the braking force is much smaller', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Smaller eddy currents give a smaller opposing force. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (The slots break up the paths of the eddy currents, so the braking force is much smaller).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('a370a075-8d3e-51de-bd27-8b820f85a49a', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 21, 21, 'The north pole of a magnet is pushed towards the end of a coil. Looking at that end from the magnet, which way does the induced current flow?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Anticlockwise, making that end a north pole that repels the magnet', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'An anticlockwise current seen from an end makes that end a north pole. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (Anticlockwise, making that end a north pole that repels the magnet).', 1, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc71048cb-t fgc71048cb-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc71048cb-t">Magnet pushed towards a coil</title><desc id="fgc71048cb-d">A bar magnet with its north pole nearest the coil is pushed towards the end of a coil connected to a galvanometer.</desc><rect x="24" y="77" width="60" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="84" y="77" width="60" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="54" y="95" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><text x="114" y="95" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><path d="M233.6,61 A6,34 0 0,0 233.6,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M233.6,61 A6,34 0 0,1 233.6,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><p