cap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="129" x2="225" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345" y1="129" x2="345" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="190" x2="273" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="297" y1="190" x2="345" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="285" cy="190" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="285" y="190.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">G</text><line x1="40" y1="55" x2="121.7" y2="55" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="128,55 119.8,58.8 119.8,51.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'A bar magnet with its north pole nearest the coil is pushed towards the end of a coil connected to a galvanometer.'),
('7962f357-6b4a-5790-9bbe-cce412c3995d', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 22, 22, 'An induced e.m.f. of 0.20 V drives a current through a 4.0 Ω resistor for 0.50 s. Calculate the energy transferred in the resistor.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.005', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'W = (V²/R)t = (0.20² ÷ 4.0) × 0.50 = 5.0 × 10⁻³ J. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: P = V²/R then × t. A1: W = 0.0050 J.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('feea2d70-0fa7-5e39-a7c7-236b156f5656', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 23, 23, 'A rod 0.20 m long moves at 4.0 m s⁻¹ across a 0.50 T field on rails joined by a 0.10 Ω resistor. Calculate the magnetic braking force on the rod.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4', 'N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = BLv = 0.50 × 0.20 × 4.0 = 0.40 V. I = 0.40 ÷ 0.10 = 4.0 A. F = BIL = 0.50 × 4.0 × 0.20 = 0.40 N. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E and I. C1: F = BIL. A1: F = 0.40 N.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg56f8412e-t fg56f8412e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg56f8412e-t">Magnetic braking</title><desc id="fg56f8412e-d">Top view: a 0.20 m rod moving at 4.0 m s⁻¹ along rails joined by a 0.10 Ω resistor, in a uniform 0.50 T field into the page. The braking force F opposes the motion.</desc><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="340" y2="70" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="180" x2="340" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="84" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="143" x2="84" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="77" y="107" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="56" y="125" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.10 Ω</text><line x1="116.1" y1="88.3" x2="124.1" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.