('0500eaef-dd74-534f-9f4b-a8f0c252838b', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 24, 24, 'A magnet of mass 0.020 kg falls down a vertical copper tube at a steady terminal speed of 0.050 m s⁻¹. Calculate the rate at which energy is dissipated in the tube, in mW. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9.81 mW', 'mW', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'At terminal speed the magnetic drag equals the weight: F = 0.020 × 9.81 = 0.196 N. P = Fv = 0.1962 × 0.050 = 0.00981 W. In mW: 0.009810 × 1000 = 9.81. Mark scheme (4 marks). B1: drag = weight. C1: P = Fv. C1: conversion. A1: P = 9.81 mW.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge2276d60-t fge2276d60-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge2276d60-t">Magnet in a copper tube</title><desc id="fge2276d60-d">A magnet of mass 0.020 kg falling down a vertical copper tube at a steady terminal speed of 0.050 m s⁻¹.</desc><rect x="110" y="30" width="60" height="270" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="118" y="30" width="44" height="270" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="110" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="142" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="140" y="126" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><text x="140" y="158" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><line x1="190" y1="120" x2="190" y2="183.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="190,190 186.2,181.8 193.8,181.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="198" y="155" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">0.050 m s⁻¹</text><text x="180" y="40" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">copper tube</text></svg>', 'A magnet of mass 0.020 kg falling down a vertical copper tube at a steady terminal speed of 0.050 m s⁻¹.'),
('00c3646b-0c3f-55fb-84ab-1da71314386e', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 25, 25, 'A magnet is dropped through a coil connected to a resistor. How does its acceleration compare with g as it passes through?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is less than g, because the induced current exerts a force opposing its motion', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Energy is transferred to the circuit, so the magnet gains kinetic energy more slowly. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: opposing force. C1: acceleration less than g. A1: A (It is less than g, because the induced current exerts a force opposing its motion).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge4684dff-t fge4684dff-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge4684dff-t">Magnet falling through a coil</title><desc id="fge4684dff-d">A bar magnet falls, north pole first, towards a coil whose ends are connected to a resistor.</desc><rect x="128" y="24" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="56" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="140" y="40" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><text x="140" y="72" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><line x1="170" y1="40" x2="170" y2="93.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,100 166.2,91.8 173.8,91.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b