('7bae4695-d5b9-5b40-89d8-8989dc5e8f73', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 26, 26, 'A rod is pushed at 2.0 m s⁻¹ across a 0.30 T field. The rod is 0.50 m long and the circuit resistance is 1.5 Ω. Using F = B²L²v/R, calculate the force needed to keep the speed constant.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.03', 'N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = B²L²v/R = 0.30² × 0.50² × 2.0 ÷ 1.5 = 0.030 N. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: formula. C1: substitution. A1: F = 0.030 N.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg8cd1bfc0-t fg8cd1bfc0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg8cd1bfc0-t">Rod on rails</title><desc id="fg8cd1bfc0-d">Top view: a 0.50 m rod pushed at 2.0 m s⁻¹ along rails across a uniform 0.30 T field into the page; the circuit resistance is 1.5 Ω.</desc><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="340" y2="70" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="180" x2="340" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="84" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="143" x2="84" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="77" y="107" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="56" y="125" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5 Ω</text><line x1="116.1" y1="88.3" x2="124.1" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-