ap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="129" x2="317.9" y2="121" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="153.7" x2="317.9" y2="161.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="161.7" x2="317.9" y2="153.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="240" y1="54" x2="240" y2="196" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="246" y1="44" x2="303.7" y2="44" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="310,44 301.8,47.8 301.8,40.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="316" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">2.0 m s⁻¹</text><polygon points="356,70 359,76.3 353,76.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="356" y1="74.9" x2="356" y2="175.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="356,180 353,173.7 359,173.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="362" y="125" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.50 m</text><line x1="20" y1="230" x2="28" y2="238" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="20" y1="238" x2="28" y2="230" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="36" y="234" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 0.30 T into the page</text></svg>', 'Top view: a 0.50 m rod pushed at 2.0 m s⁻¹ along rails across a uniform 0.30 T field into the page; the circuit resistance is 1.5 Ω.'),
('44e393cb-39f0-544f-8ee7-c5a33a65a2ea', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 27, 27, 'The south pole of a magnet is pulled away from the end of a coil. What pole forms at that end of the coil?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A north pole, which attracts the retreating south pole', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The coil opposes the decrease of flux by attracting the magnet. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: oppose decrease. C1: north attracts south. A1: D (A north pole, which attracts the retreating south pole).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg04283b95-t fg04283b95-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg04283b95-t">Magnet pulled away from a coil</title><desc id="fg04283b95-d">A bar magnet with its south pole nearest a coil is pulled away from the coil, which is connected to a galvanometer.</desc><rect x="24" y="77" width="60" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="84" y="77" width="60" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="54" y="95" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><text x="114" y="95" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><path d="M233.6,61 A6,34 0 0,0 233.6,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M233.6,61 A6,34 0 0,1 233.6,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M250.7,61 A6,34 0 0,0 250.7,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M250.7,61 A6,34 0 0,1 250.7,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M267.9,61 A6,34 0 0,0 267.9,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M267.9,61 A6,34 0 0,1 267.9,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M285,61 A6,34 0 0,0 285,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M285,61 A6,34 0 0,1 285,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M302.1,61 A6,34 0 0,0 302.1,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M302.1,61 A6,34 0 0,1 302.1,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M319.3,61 A6,34 0 0,0 319.3,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M319.3,61 A6,34 0 0,1 319.3,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M336.4,61 A6,34 0 0,0 336.4,129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M336.4,61 A6,34 0 0,1 336.4,129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="95" x2="225" y2="129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345" y1="95" x2="345" y2="129" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="129" x2="225" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345" y1="129" x2="345" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="190" x2="273" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="297" y1="190" x2="345" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="285" cy="190" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="285" y="190.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">G</text><line x1="128" y1="55" x2="46.3" y2="55" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="40,55 48.2,51.2 48.2,58.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'A bar magnet with its south pole nearest a coil is pulled away from the coil, which is connected to a galvanometer.'),
('f0deffc3-6926-57a0-a306-ba3cdd9b0e4a', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 28, 28, 'A coil is pulled out of a field, generating 0.075 V for 0.20 s in a circuit of resistance 0.50 Ω. Calculate the energy dissipated, in mJ.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.25 mJ', 'mJ', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = V²/R = 0.075² ÷ 0.50 = 0.0112 W. W = Pt = 0.01125 × 0.20 = 0.00225 J. In mJ: 0.002250 × 1000 = 2.25. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: P = V²/R. C1: W = Pt. A1: W = 2.25 mJ.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4a907cda-5fde-5dd3-8b29-cc9449834c0e', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 29, 29, 'A small generator needs a mechanical input of 50 W and delivers 42 W of electrical power. Calculate its efficiency.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '84', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Efficiency = 42 ÷ 50 × 100 = 84 %. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: useful out ÷ total in. C1: percentage. A1: efficiency = 84%.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('dd93d85f-56bc-5122-9401-f4c7c310488c', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 30, 30, 'Why can magnetic (eddy-current) brakes slow a train but not hold it stationary?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The braking force depends on the speed, so it falls to zero as the train stops', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Induced e.m.f. ∝ v, so the current and force fall as v falls. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: e.m.f. ∝ v. C1: force ∝ v. C1: zero at rest. A1: B (The braking force depends on the speed, so it falls to zero as the train stops).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('bdfbd20c-40b3-5682-b701-bf7f0da69962', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 31, 31, 'An e.m.f. of 0.10 V is induced around an eddy-current path of resistance 0.010 Ω in a metal block. Calculate the power dissipated.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = E²/R = 0.10² ÷ 0.010 = 1.0 W. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: P = E²/R. C1: value. A1: P = 1.0 W.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2be395ba-232b-57d5-ac71-ad3a04b42958', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 32, 32, 'Why are transformer cores made of thin insulated sheets (laminations) rather than solid iron?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The insulation breaks up eddy-current paths, reducing energy wasted as heat', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Smaller loops of higher resistance carry much smaller eddy currents. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: breaks eddy-current paths. C1: less heating. A1: C (The insulation breaks up eddy-current paths, reducing energy wasted as heat).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f0aee544-af7e-56df-8170-beb015e70f24', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 33, 33, 'A rod 0.50 m long moves at 3.0 m s⁻¹ across a 0.20 T field, in a circuit of resistance 0.50 Ω. Using P = B²L²v²/R, calculate the electrical power produced.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.18', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = B²L²v²/R = 0.20² × 0.50² × 3.0² ÷ 0.50 = 0.18 W. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: formula. C1: substitution. A1: P = 0.18 W.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f268d324-cd08-53fa-b70f-a038f0299761', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 34, 34, 'A switch in the primary circuit of two coils on an iron core is closed. Which statement about the current induced in the secondary is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It flows briefly, in a direction whose field opposes the growing flux', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The secondary opposes the change in flux, and only while it changes. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: brief current. C1: opposes growth. A1: A (It flows briefly, in a direction whose field opposes the growing flux).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1716c9fb-t fg1716c9fb-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1716c9fb-t">Two coils on an iron core</title><desc id="fg1716c9fb-d">Two coils on an iron core. The primary is connected to a cell through a switch that is about to be closed; the secondary is connected to a galvanometer.</desc><path d="M150,46 a6,6 0 0,1 6,-6 h138 a6,6 0 0,1 6,6 v148 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,6 h-138 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,-6 Z M180,70 h90 v100 h-90 Z" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));fill-rule:evenodd;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="184" y2="96" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="100" x2="184" y2="106" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="110" x2="184" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="120" x2="184" y2="126" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="130" x2="184" y2="136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="140" x2="184" y2="146" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="150" x2="184" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="137" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113" y1="90" x2="100" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="156" x2="100" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="90" x2="100" y2="118" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="128" x2="100" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="87" y1="118" x2="113" y2="118" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="128" x2="107" y2="128" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="90" x2="304" y2="96" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="100" x2="304" y2="106" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="110" x2="304" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="120" x2="304" y2="126" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="130" x2="304" y2="136" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="140" x2="304" y2="146" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="150" x2="304" y2="156" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="90" x2="370" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="156" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="90" x2="370" y2="111" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="135" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="370" cy="123" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="370" y="123.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">G</text><circle cx="113" cy="90" r="2.6" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="137" cy="90" r="2.6" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="113" y1="90" x2="135" y2="79" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Two coils on an iron core. The primary is connected to a cell through a switch that is about to be closed; the secondary is connected to a galvanometer.'),
('5cb1b392-5358-54f8-9802-741c49ab6991', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 35, 35, 'A rod circuit dissipates 0.18 W when the rod moves at 3.0 m s⁻¹. Calculate the power at 6.0 m s⁻¹, given P = B²L²v²/R.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.72', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P ∝ v²: P = 0.18 × (6.0 ÷ 3.0)² = 0.72 W. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: P ∝ v². C1: ratio squared. C1: value. A1: P = 0.72 W.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('3b099ea9-d1e8-54e1-b5ff-b2a99dfb6f26', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 36, 36, 'A switch carrying a large current through a coil is opened, and a spark jumps across it. Which explanation is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The collapsing flux induces a large e.m.f. in the coil, which tries to keep the current flowing', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Lenz''s law: the induced e.m.f. opposes the fall in current. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: rapid flux change. C1: e.m.f. opposes fall in current. A1: D (The collapsing flux induces a large e.m.f. in the coil, which tries to keep the current flowing).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f09a9973-3e62-58ca-bd51-fbf225497255', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 37, 37, 'A 0.050 kg magnet falls 0.80 m from rest through a coil and reaches 3.6 m s⁻¹. Calculate the energy transferred to the circuit, ignoring air resistance. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.0684', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Loss of GPE = 0.050 × 9.81 × 0.80 = 0.392 J. KE = 0.5 × 0.050 × 3.6² = 0.324 J. Energy to circuit = 0.3924 − 0.3240 = 0.0684 J. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: GPE lost. C1: KE gained. A1: E = 0.0684 J.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg95df634f-t fg95df634f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg95df634f-t">Magnet falling through a coil</title><desc id="fg95df634f-d">A 0.050 kg magnet is released from rest 0.80 m above a coil connected to a galvanometer and falls through it.</desc><rect x="128" y="24" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="56" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="140" y="40" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><text x="140" y="72" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><line x1="170" y1="40" x2="170" y2="93.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,100 166.2,91.8 173.8,91.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="178" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor