('dff1fdfe-0047-5771-a1d4-1cee06ab015b', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 39, 39, 'A loop of resistance 0.25 Ω must carry 0.80 A. It is a 0.20 m rod sliding on rails in a 0.50 T field. Calculate the speed needed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = IR = 0.80 × 0.25 = 0.20 V. v = E/(BL) = 0.20 ÷ (0.50 × 0.20) = 2.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E = IR. C1: v = E/(BL). A1: v = 2.0 m s⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg961c8a91-t fg961c8a91-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg961c8a91-t">Rod on rails</title><desc id="fg961c8a91-d">Top view: a 0.20 m rod sliding along rails in a uniform 0.50 T field into the page; the loop resistance is 0.25 Ω and the current must be 0.80 A.</desc><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="340" y2="70" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="180" x2="340" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="84" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="143" x2="84" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="77" y="107" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="56" y="125" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.25 Ω</text><line x1="116.1" y1="88.3" x2="124.1" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"