('73b71b10-b46e-54d9-bd5e-f2791166142a', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 42, 42, 'A metal rod 0.20 m long rests across horizontal rails joined by a 0.10 Ω resistor. A uniform field of 0.50 T points vertically downwards. The rod is pushed east at 4.0 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the e.m.f. and the current. (b) Use Lenz''s law to state the direction of the magnetic force on the rod. (c) Calculate this force. (d) Calculate the power needed to keep the rod moving. Give only the answer to (d).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.6', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 0.50 × 0.20 × 4.0 = 0.40 V; I = 0.40 ÷ 0.10 = 4.0 A. (b) Westwards, opposing the motion. (c) F = BIL = 0.50 × 4.0 × 0.20 = 0.40 N. (d) P = Fv = 0.40 × 4.0 = 1.6 W, equal to EI = 0.40 × 4.0. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E and I. B1: force opposes motion. C1: F = BIL. C1: P = Fv. B1: equals EI. A1: P = 1.6 W.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbd0fd067-t fgbd0fd067-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbd0fd067-t">Rod pushed east</title><desc id="fgbd0fd067-d">Top view with north up the page: a 0.20 m rod across rails joined by a 0.10 Ω resistor; a 0.50 T field points vertically downwards (into the page) and the rod is pushed east at 4.0 m s⁻¹.</desc><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="340" y2="70" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="180" x2="340" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="70" x2="84" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84" y1="143" x2="84" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="77" y="107" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="56" y="125" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.10 Ω</text><line x1="116.1" y1="88.3" x2="124.1" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="116.1" y1="96.3" x2="124.1" y2="88.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="116.1" y1="121" x2="124.1" y2="129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="116.1" y1="129" x2="124.1" y2="121" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="116.1" y1="153.7" x2="124.1" y2="161.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="116.1" y1="161.7" x2="124.1" y2="153.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="148.4" y1="88.3" x2="156.4" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="148.4" y1="96.3" x2="156.4" y2="88.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="148.4" y1="121" x2="156.4" y2="129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="148.4" y1="129" x2="156.4" y2="121" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="148.4" y1="153.7" x2="156.4" y2="161.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280