nd;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="88.3" x2="317.9" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="96.3" x2="317.9" y2="88.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="121" x2="317.9" y2="129" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="129" x2="317.9" y2="121" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="153.7" x2="317.9" y2="161.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.9" y1="161.7" x2="317.9" y2="153.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="240" y1="54" x2="240" y2="196" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="246" y1="44" x2="303.7" y2="44" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="310,44 301.8,47.8 301.8,40.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="316" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">4.0 m s⁻¹ east</text><polygon points="356,70 359,76.3 353,76.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="356" y1="74.9" x2="356" y2="175.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="356,180 353,173.7 359,173.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="362" y="125" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.20 m</text><line x1="20" y1="230" x2="28" y2="238" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="20" y1="238" x2="28" y2="230" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="36" y="234" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 0.50 T downwards (into the page)</text><line x1="28" y1="56" x2="28" y2="28.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="28,24 31,30.3 25,30.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="28" y="15" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">N</text></svg>', 'Top view with north up the page: a 0.20 m rod across rails joined by a 0.10 Ω resistor; a 0.50 T field points vertically downwards (into the page) and the rod is pushed east at 4.0 m s⁻¹.'),
('34004924-7a99-5828-8744-c1bc96e9e28e', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 43, 43, 'A strong magnet of mass 0.040 kg falls down a vertical copper tube. The magnetic drag force is proportional to its speed, F = kv, with k = 2.0 N s m⁻¹. (a) Explain why there is a drag force. (b) Calculate the terminal speed. Give only the answer to (b). Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.1962', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) The falling magnet changes the flux through the tube, inducing eddy currents whose fields oppose its motion. (b) At terminal speed kv = mg, so v = 0.040 × 9.81 ÷ 2.0 = 0.196 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: eddy currents in tube. B1: oppose motion. M1: kv = mg. C1: value. A1: v = 0.196 m s⁻¹.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgab009627-t fgab009627-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgab009627-t">Magnet in a copper tube</title><desc id="fgab009627-d">A strong magnet of mass 0.040 kg falling down a vertical copper tube; a magnetic drag force F = kv acts upwards on it.</desc><rect x="110" y="30" width="60" height="270" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="118" y="30" width="44" height="270" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="110" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="128" y="142" width="24" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="140" y="126" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">S</text><text x="140" y="158" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">N</text><line x1="190" y1="120" x2="190" y2="183.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="190,190 186.2,181.8 193.8,181.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="198" y="155" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">v</text><text x="180" y="40" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">copper tube</text></svg>', 'A strong magnet of mass 0.040 kg falling down a vertical copper tube; a magnetic drag force F = kv acts upwards on it.'),
('0d5f75dc-023e-57c5-aca9-33c8d80a4e10', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 44, 44, 'An eddy-current brake on a 4.0 × 10⁴ kg train gives a drag force F = cv, with c = 4000 N s m⁻¹. The train is moving at 30 m s⁻¹ and no other force acts. (a) Calculate the initial deceleration. (b) Show that the speed falls exponentially with time constant m/c. (c) Calculate the speed 10 s later. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '11.04', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = cv/m = 4000 × 30 ÷ 4.0 × 10⁴ = 3.0 m s⁻². (b) m dv/dt = −cv gives v = v₀e^(−ct/m), with time constant m/c = 4.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 4000 = 10 s. (c) v = 30 × e^(−10/10) = 11.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: a = F/m. M1: m dv/dt = −cv. B1: exponential decay. C1: time constant. C1: value. A1: v = 11.0 m s⁻¹.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('3ab21c68-c666-5441-9de6-18ef2a294148', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 45, 45, 'A coil is pulled at a steady 0.50 m s⁻¹ out of a magnetic field against a magnetic force of 0.040 N, through a distance of 0.10 m. (a) Calculate the work done. (b) State where this energy ends up. (c) Calculate the power needed, in mW. Give only the answer to (a), in mJ.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4 mJ', 'mJ', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) W = Fd = 0.040 × 0.10 = 4.0 × 10⁻³ J. In mJ: 4.0 × 10⁻³ × 1000 = 4.0. (b) As internal energy (heat) in the coil''s resistance. (c) P = Fv = 0.040 × 0.50 = 0.020 W, which is 20 mW. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: W = Fd. C1: conversion. B1: heating of coil. C1: P = Fv. A1: W = 4.0 mJ.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg3323ba90-t fg3323ba90-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg3323ba90-t">Coil pulled out of a field</title><desc id="fg3323ba90-d">Top view: a coil partly inside a region of uniform magnetic field into the page, pulled out at a steady 0.50 m s⁻¹ against a magnetic force of 0.040 N over 0.10 m.</desc><rect x="220" y="50" width="186" height="160" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="231.5" y1="62" x2="239.5" y2="70" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="231.5" y1="70" x2="239.5" y2="62" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="231.5" y1="94" x2="239.5" y2="102" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoi