('7ed23bb3-fb38-58d1-99f0-289e4eef5511', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 46, 46, 'A rectangular loop of mass 0.010 kg and resistance 0.020 Ω falls vertically with its plane at right angles to a horizontal field of 0.50 T. Its lower side, 0.10 m long, is in the field while its upper side is outside. (a) Show that the magnetic force on the loop is B²L²v/R. (b) Calculate the terminal speed. Give only the answer to (b). Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.7848', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = BLv, I = BLv/R, F = BIL = B²L²v/R, upwards. (b) mg = B²L²v/R, so v = mgR/(B²L²) = 0.010 × 9.81 × 0.020 ÷ (0.50² × 0.10²) = 0.785 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: E = BLv. M1: F = BIL. B1: B²L²v/R. C1: equated to mg. C1: value. A1: v = 0.785 m s⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg60c60485-t fg60c60485-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg60c60485-t">Loop falling into a field</title><desc id="fg60c60485-d">A rectangular loop falling vertically with its plane at right angles to a horizontal 0.50 T field (into the page). Its 0.10 m lower side is inside the field region; its upper side is outside.</desc><rect x="30" y="150" width="360" height="76" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="41" y1="165" x2="49" y2="173" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="41" y1="173" x2="49" y2="165" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="41" y1="203" x2="49" y2="211" style="stroke:var(--fig