="32" y1="242" x2="40" y2="250" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="32" y1="250" x2="40" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="48" y="246" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 0.50 T into the page</text></svg>', 'A rectangular loop falling vertically with its plane at right angles to a horizontal 0.50 T field (into the page). Its 0.10 m lower side is inside the field region; its upper side is outside.'),
('68692984-aa60-516f-8d0b-57334dd1930a', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 47, 47, 'In a jumping-ring demonstration, an aluminium ring of mass 5.0 g leaps 0.40 m into the air. (a) Calculate the gravitational potential energy it gains. (b) Only 2.0 % of the electrical energy supplied to the coil in the pulse reaches the ring''s motion. Calculate the energy supplied. Give only the answer to (a). Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.01962', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) ΔE_p = mgh = 5.0 × 10⁻³ × 9.81 × 0.40 = 0.0196 J. (b) Energy supplied = 0.01962 ÷ 0.020 = 0.981 J. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: mgh. C1: mass in kg. C1: ÷ 0.020. B1: most energy heats the coil and ring. A1: E_p = 0.0196 J.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('23357ce7-28da-5fbd-8151-5c39188f2170', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 48, 48, 'A long solenoid has 2000 turns per metre, and its current increases at 10 A s⁻¹. A 20-turn coil of area 1.0 × 10⁻³ m² and resistance 0.50 Ω is placed inside, face-on to the field. (a) Calculate the rate of change of B, using B = µ₀nI. (b) Calculate the e.m.f. induced in the coil. (c) Calculate the induced current, in mA, and state its direction relative to the solenoid current. Give only the current from (c). Take µ₀ = 4π × 10⁻⁷ H m⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.005 mA', 'mA', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) dB/dt = 4π × 10⁻⁷ × 2000 × 10 = 0.0251 T s⁻¹. (b) E = NA dB/dt = 20 × 1.0 × 10⁻³ × 0.02513 = 5.03 × 10⁻⁴ V. (c) I = 5.027 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 0.50 = 0.00101 A. In mA: 0.001005 × 1000 = 1.01. It circulates opposite to the solenoid current, opposing the increase. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: dB/dt. C1: E = NA dB/dt. C1: I = E/R. C1: conversion. B1: opposite direction by Lenz. A1: I = 1.01 mA.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg47297ffd-t fg47297ffd-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg47297ffd-t">Coil inside a solenoid</title><desc id="fg47297ffd-d">A long solenoid with 2000 turns per metre whose current increases at 10 A s⁻¹; a 20-turn coil of area 1.0 × 10⁻³ m² and resistance 0.50 Ω sits inside, face-on to the field.</desc><path d="M69.4,50 A6,40 0 0,0 69.4,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M69.4,50 A6,40 0 0,1 69.4,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M88.1,50 A6,40 0 0,0 88.1,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M88.1,50 A6,40 0 0,1 88.1,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M106.9,50 A6,40 0 0,0 106.9,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M106.9,50 A6,40 0 0,1 106.9,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M125.6,50 A6,40 0 0,0 125.6,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M125.6,50 A6,40 0 0,1 125.6,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M144.4,50 A6,40 0 0,0 144.4,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M144.4,50 A6,40 0 0,1 144.4,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M163.1,50 A6,40 0 0,0 163.1,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M163.1,50 A6,40 0 0,1 163.1,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M181.9,50 A6,40 0 0,0 181.9,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M181.9,50 A6,40 0 0,1 181.9,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M200.6,50 A6,40 0 0,0 200.6,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M200.6,50 A6,40 0 0,1 200.6,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M219.4,50 A6,40 0 0,0 219.4,130" style="st