ound"/><path d="M350.6,50 A6,40 0 0,0 350.6,130" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M350.6,50 A6,40 0 0,1 350.6,130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="60" y1="50" x2="40" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="360" y1="130" x2="380" y2="130" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M197.2,72 A6,18 0 0,0 197.2,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M197.2,72 A6,18 0 0,1 197.2,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M205.8,72 A6,18 0 0,0 205.8,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M205.8,72 A6,18 0 0,1 205.8,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M214.2,72 A6,18 0 0,0 214.2,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M214.2,72 A6,18 0 0,1 214.2,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M222.8,72 A6,18 0 0,0 222.8,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M222.8,72 A6,18 0 0,1 222.8,108" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="210" y="166" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">solenoid: 2000 turns per metre, current rising at 10 A s⁻¹</text><text x="210" y="186" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">20-turn coil, area 1.0 × 10⁻³ m², 0.50 Ω</text></svg>', 'A long solenoid with 2000 turns per metre whose current increases at 10 A s⁻¹; a 20-turn coil of area 1.0 × 10⁻³ m² and resistance 0.50 Ω sits inside, face-on to the field.'),
('797ff6ad-484e-5acd-b9dc-a82f06c86073', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 49, 49, 'A small generator turning at 100 rad s⁻¹ lights a lamp that takes 0.30 A at 20 V. (a) Calculate the electrical power. (b) Explain why the generator becomes harder to turn when the lamp is connected. (c) Calculate the extra torque needed, ignoring losses. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.06', 'N m', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = VI = 20 × 0.30 = 6.0 W. (b) The current in the coil feels a magnetic force opposing its rotation (Lenz''s law). (c) P = τω, so τ = 6.0 ÷ 100 = 0.060 N m. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: P = VI. B1: opposing force on coil current. M1: P = τω. C1: value. A1: τ = 0.060 N m.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('ed6b3d72-e38b-521f-8629-e97011badb2b', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '4ac2239b-8226-4bfc-8116-0d8626521f30', 'a-level', '26.4', '9702 coursebook 26.4 · Lenz''s law', 50, 50, 'A pendulum with a copper bob swings between the poles of a magnet and loses 15 % of its energy on each swing because of eddy currents. Its initial energy is 0.050 J. (a) Explain why energy is lost. (b) Calculate its energy after 5 swings. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.02219', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Eddy currents induced in the moving bob oppose its motion and heat it. (b) E = 0.050 × 0.85⁵ = 0.0222 J. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: eddy currents oppose motion. B1: energy to heat. M1: × 0.85 each swing. C1: value. A1: E = 0.0222 J.', 5, NULL, NULL)
INSERT INTO problem_options (id, problem_id, option_text, option_letter, is_correct, "order") VALUES
('fdad3a56-5e10-5ba6-8b2d-9119af4cc2ca', 'c127d16f-6f40-59e0-9078-b49a96fb1a9a', 'Always clockwise', 'A', false, 0),
('032e66cc-5513-5cc6-83ff-54b7fa41ed1b', 'c127d16f-6f40-59e0-9078-b49a96fb1a9a', 'Such that it increases the change in flux', 'B', false, 1),
('ad031cb7-d598-56f5-9705-d8e39e25617c', 'c127d16f-6f40-59e0-9078-b49a96fb1a9a', 'Such that its magnetic field opposes the change in flux that produces it', 'C', true, 2),
('449deafc-eff5-5180-a64d-dd3f4d7d7b44', 'c127d16f-6f40-59e0-9078-b49a96fb1a9a', 'Always from north to south', 'D', false, 3),
('aa39180f-d346-52ec-85fd-8cddaa114eff', 'ae5c18b4-44b0-51d9-88bc-0b14ad275597', 'A south pole, which attracts the magnet and opposes its removal', 'A', true, 0),
('588b09db-8498-55ff-b05b-b6b0601f3257', 'ae5c18b4-44b0-51d9-88bc-0b14ad275597', 'A north pole, which repels the magnet', 'B', false, 1),
('7f99cb57-8247-5b2e-96b4-7a9a68e60184', 'ae5c18b4-44b0-51d9-88bc-0b14ad275597', 'No pole forms', 'C', false, 2),
('e2bd11a5-57f3-50af-ab72-941a1087419e', 'ae5c18b4-44b0-51d9-88bc-0b14ad275597', 'A north pole, which attracts the magnet', 'D', false, 3),
('13f1ec90-733e-5bd8-9d0e-b95a799da984', '5d30639b-b46b-54e4-b3e7-f69644589320', 'From the magnet''s own energy store, which runs down', 'A', false, 0),
('2124286c-4f6d-5846-81fa-1d0cf5f5c3fb', '5d30639b-b46b-54e4-b3e7-f69644589320', 'From nowhere: it is created', 'B', false, 1),
('69eaac62-879e-545e-8894-cbecaab23b4e', '5d30639b-b46b-54e4-b3e7-f69644589320', 'From the heating of the coil', 'C', false, 2),
('d93840fe-e208-5aa7-981d-062753bab4bd', '5d30639b-b46b-54e4-b3e7-f69644589320', 'From the work done against the opposing magnetic force', 'D', true, 3),
('eeff7626-627e-5fce-b674-2ff13a3ccaaf', 'cb08bc14-02f0-54ba-97ce-3109858bad49', 'The direction of the induced current', 'A', false, 0),
('032b08a3-046d-5901-b2df-e3d7a4a61cb1', 'cb08bc14-02f0-54ba-97ce-3109858bad49', 'The direction of motion of the conductor', 'B', true, 1),
('e38349e8-44bb-5439-89aa-ab852c66bc9c', 'cb08bc14-02f0-54ba-97ce-3109858bad49', 'The direction of the field', 'C', false, 2),
('dc0c014f-1bb3-5f6b-be01-6b276fafc0ad', 'cb08bc14-02f0-54ba-97ce-3109858bad49', 'The direction of the force on the conductor', 'D', false, 3),
('2ccd1d13-4613-5411-9b6b-e4bf95f6bf0f', '1435043a-d7d4-55d9-8a47-e9becfcf5133', 'The ring is attracted by the iron', 'A', false, 0),
('3c8d8d87-b57a-5ff9-bff5-f931b8988646', '1435043a-d7d4-55d9-8a47-e9becfcf5133', 'The ring becomes a permanent magnet', 'B', false, 1),
('f0bccc6a-4cef-5675-9b48-438b285f472d', '1435043a-d7d4-55d9-8a47-e9becfcf5133', 'The induced current in the ring produces a field that opposes the growing flux, so the ring is repelled', 'C', true, 2),
('00cd50cc-3bb2-5e0a-be27-826cd68aba88', '1435043a-d7d4-55d9-8a47-e9becfcf5133', 'The ring is heated and expands', 'D', false, 3),
('60fa2844-a46f-510f-8291-7c92b4cded44', 'ea0caf6a-5e25-545c-b684-264f3521a4f3', 'Induced currents that circulate inside a solid conductor when the flux through it changes', 'A', true, 0),
('414371f4-de13-5026-92f7-529543b4e9a9', 'ea0caf6a-5e25-545c-b684-264f3521a4f3', 'Currents in a superconductor', 'B', false, 1),
('45e18b83-96c4-5e48-8c67-969e6b8e8b3e', 'ea0caf6a-5e25-545c-b684-264f3521a4f3', 'Currents caused by heating', 'C', false, 2),
('37c64db6-52e7-5412-a48e-245d9943bee9', 'ea0caf6a-5e25-545c-b684-264f3521a4f3', 'Currents that flow only in coils', 'D', false, 3),
('554207e2-5df4-5a99-b696-8df66d6c9edc', 'd7d9f764-dc29-5006-b8dc-047baa23fe0a', 'Because currents always flow clockwise', 'A', false, 0),
('e826c8f3-9306-5ef7-bd1b-f51d3f6af65b', 'd7d9f764-dc29-5006-b8dc-047baa23fe0a', 'Because magnets always repel', 'B', false, 1),
('df17c930-2130-534f-883b-9f0705b1aec1', 'd7d9f764-dc29-5006-b8dc-047baa23fe0a', 'Because flux cannot change', 'C', false, 2),
('a8b11e77-5326-55e9-bab1-a270856e1995', 'd7d9f764-dc29-5006-b8dc-047baa23fe0a', 'Otherwise energy would be created from nothing, breaking the principle of conservation of energy', 'D', true, 3),
('e359c3dd-7b0e-5cb4-96aa-0d813af37cf8', '200b548d-7820-5720-90ef-558bd62bfaa1', 'The slotted plate is heavier', 'A', false, 0),
('18e6a3cd-bea0-5e04-a8a3-cb4983093b4f', '200b548d-7820-5720-90ef-558bd62bfaa1', 'The slots break up the paths of the eddy currents, so the braking force is much smaller', 'B', true, 1),
('707f9f0e-d26a-5c6f-8fdd-3def21458911', '200b548d-7820-5720-90ef-558bd62bfaa1', 'The slots make the plate magnetic', 'C', false, 2),
('3d5cd7b7-ce29-5716-a6f8-6c51fbf74b24', '200b548d-7820-5720-90ef-558bd62bfaa1', 'The slotted plate has more resistance to air', 'D', false, 3),
('6142eacc-e4ff-515e-9cbf-af100cba15ac', 'a370a075-8d3e-51de-bd27-8b820f85a49a', 'Clockwise, making that end a south pole', 'A', false, 0),
('43cb1c30-e2b8-547d-a8bb-1271e8faa92e', 'a370a075-8d3e-51de-bd27-8b820f85a49a', 'No current flows', 'B', false, 1),
('666221e1-e405-5de4-9908-7f3dda1b0954', 'a370a075-8d3e-51de-bd27-8b820f85a49a', 'Anticlockwise, making that end a north pole that repels the magnet', 'C', true, 2),
('9784f606-8fc1-5152-a7fa-5061fda683fd', 'a370a075-8d3e-51de-bd27-8b820f85a49a', 'Clockwise, making that end a north pole', 'D', false, 3),
('aaf863ad-dd71-5513-ae16-9ec9e3babac0', '00c3646b-0c3f-55fb-84ab-1da71314386e', 'It is less than g, because the induced current exerts a force opposing its motion', 'A', true, 0),
('50483e6f-1742-52e2-a89b-b4759a000ee9', '00c3646b-0c3f-55fb-84ab-1da71314386e', 'It is greater than g', 'B', false, 1),
('f6c161de-06a6-52fb-8a29-483d55126ca2', '00c3646b-0c3f-55fb-84ab-1da71314386e', 'It equals g', 'C', false, 2),
('32d3efae-d22c-59cf-957d-b939a3a682dd', '00c3646b-0c3f-55fb-84ab-1da71314386e', 'It is zero', 'D', false, 3),
('dc17f926-e700-5998-bdc3-dfeb4edef4aa', '44e393cb-39f0-544f-8ee7-c5a33a65a2ea', 'A south pole, which repels it', 'A', false, 0),
('24509548-716a-5b75-8684-603bc2acaa95', '44e393cb-39f0-544f-8ee7-c5a33a65a2ea', 'No pole forms', 'B', false, 1),
('777c6f47-525a-51e2-8323-087fbd0ef8a1', '44e393cb-39f0-544f-8ee7-c5a33a65a2ea', 'A south pole, which attracts it', 'C', false, 2),
('312a5c3e-72ab-53af-99fb-ab60625556a8', '44e393cb-39f0-544f-8ee7-c5a33a65a2ea', 'A north pole, which attracts the retreating south pole', 'D', true, 3),
('2f60bf0b-b5f5-5934-b789-4bbd99c7d4a8', 'dd93d85f-56bc-5122-9401-f4c7c310488c', 'The magnets lose their magnetism when hot', 'A', false, 0),
('8f0f4731-3d8b-5372-af82-23659437cb34', 'dd93d85f-56bc-5122-9401-f4c7c310488c', 'The braking force depends on the speed, so it falls to zero as the train stops', 'B', true, 1),
('674903f1-7395-59a6-88f3-e03a16258bce', 'dd93d85f-56bc-5122-9401-f4c7c310488c', 'The brakes only work in one direction', 'C', false, 2),
('0805d243-37c6-5080-9522-4740a6dc322f', 'dd93d85f-56bc-5122-9401-f4c7c310488c', 'The eddy currents grow as the train slows', 'D', false, 3),
('f9e7e147-2971-525f-9b30-99e1181b9d0f', '2be395ba-232b-57d5-ac71-ad3a04b42958', 'To make the core stronger', 'A', false, 0),
('1db71478-f46d-562b-ac2d-5814b7955f44', '2be395ba-232b-57d5-ac71-ad3a04b42958', 'To increase the eddy currents', 'B', false, 1),
('ac5a0c98-0f2d-5e08-ab45-4450e4c43a66', '2be395ba-232b-57d5-ac71-ad3a04b42958', 'The insulation breaks up eddy-current paths, reducing energy wasted as heat', 'C', true, 2),
('37860355-ac42-51a7-b1c4-454fce13b1b8', '2be395ba-232b-57d5-ac71-ad3a04b42958', 'To reduce the magnetic flux', 'D', false, 3),
('848fb884-4c5b-5618-af70-9ac07d327207', 'f268d324-cd08-53fa-b70f-a038f0299761', 'It flows briefly, in a direction whose field opposes the growing flux', 'A', true, 0),
('7ce37442-747f-5746-8935-28183a799fe4', 'f268d324-cd08-53fa-b70f-a038f0299761', 'It flows steadily while the switch stays closed', 'B', false, 1),
('559c1c43-1537-5acc-b164-b1a67afccd70', 'f268d324-cd08-53fa-b70f-a038f0299761', 'It flows in a direction that increases the flux', 'C', false, 2),
('1f13b760-90f4-5584-b150-eb06328a088f', 'f268d324-cd08-53fa-b70f-a038f0299761', 'No current is induced', 'D', false, 3),
('bc45d87e-31f7-59bc-9cbe-38a57bd670ae', '3b099ea9-d1e8-54e1-b5ff-b2a99dfb6f26', 'The battery voltage suddenly increases', 'A', false, 0),
('bfa87dc0-f226-5da4-8144-fbd10a4edafa', '3b099ea9-d1e8-54e1-b5ff-b2a99dfb6f26', 'The coil becomes a capacitor', 'B', false, 1),
('81e2b9ac-dc0d-55af-b3e0-42acd37bb4ed', '3b099ea9-d1e8-54e1-b5ff-b2a99dfb6f26', 'The air in the switch is heated by the current', 'C', false, 2),
('acbcd2e3-5512-5c63-a24d-de54cc0d1f58', '3b099ea9-d1e8-54e1-b5ff-b2a99dfb6f26', 'The collapsing flux induces a large e.m.f. in the coil, which tries to keep the current flowing', 'D', true, 3),
('45bb9e98-b15e-52ec-aa23-069aba499d4e', 'c66dc415-35f3-50f2-8cd6-f4d8913ac3f0', 'It jumps higher than a complete ring', 'A', false, 0),
('af4b963d-7ea4-5acb-93ea-3a8e99dd222c', 'c66dc415-35f3-50f2-8cd6-f4d8913ac3f0', 'It does not jump, because no current can circulate round the ring', 'B', true, 1),
('7e4fe73e-3c59-5845-a911-afa3b70ad39c', 'c66dc415-35f3-50f2-8cd6-f4d8913ac3f0', 'It jumps the same height', 'C', false, 2),
('7562994c-bced-5550-8b9e-5b7d9b35c997', 'c66dc415-35f3-50f2-8cd6-f4d8913ac3f0', 'It is pulled down onto the coil', 'D', false, 3),
('8650d890-dd0a-5535-bc3e-c3494e465338', 'a69b3d2c-d9b9-5aea-aac9-9afe565b906f', 'A repulsion, speeding it up', 'A', false, 0),
('23823149-c8c6-5abc-9f79-31cb0e251947', 'a69b3d2c-d9b9-5aea-aac9-9afe565b906f', 'No force', 'B', false, 1),
('bc96c9b1-5afb-5ce6-a427-0b14253b5a8c', 'a69b3d2c-d9b9-5aea-aac9-9afe565b906f', 'An attraction, opposing the magnet''s removal', 'C', true, 2),
('6414cae4-a4b2-538c-adef-c1d2235f35f0', 'a69b3d2c-d9b9-5aea-aac9-9afe565b906f', 'A force at right angles to its motion', 'D', false, 3)
