width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="150" x2="304" y2="156" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="90" x2="370" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="156" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="90" x2="370" y2="105" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="141" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="363" y="105" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="398" y="123" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.0 V</text><text x="165" y="222" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">primary</text><text x="285" y="222" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">secondary</text></svg>', 'A transformer with a 230 V a.c. supply across the primary and an output of 5.0 V across the secondary.'),
('42863a78-e6e2-5704-bf09-8901e8e40203', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 10, 10, 'Why is the iron core of a transformer laminated?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'To reduce eddy currents and the energy they waste', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Thin insulated layers break up eddy-current loops. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (To reduce eddy currents and the energy they waste).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('87a57886-ac5b-59f1-ae24-5ec34f7faac9', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 11, 11, 'An ideal transformer draws 0.10 A from a 230 V supply and gives 11.5 V at its secondary. Calculate the secondary current.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'A', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'VₚIₚ = VₛIₛ, so Iₛ = 230 × 0.10 ÷ 11.5 = 2.0 A. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: power in = power out. A1: Iₛ = 2.0 A.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4363dd03-t fg4363dd03-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4363dd03-t">Ideal transformer</title><desc id="fg4363dd03-d">An ideal transformer drawing 0.10 A from a 230 V supply; the secondary gives 11.5 V across a load.</desc><path d="M150,46 a6,6 0 0,1 6,-6 h138 a6,6 0 0,1 6,6 v148 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,6 h-138 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,-6 Z M180,70 h90 v100 h-90 Z" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));fill-rule:evenodd;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="184" y2="96" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="100" x2="184" y2="106" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="110" x2="184" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="120" x2="184" y2="126" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="130" x2="184" y2="136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="140" x2="184" y2="146" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="150" x2="184" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="100" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="156" x2="100" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="90" x2="100" y2="111" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="135" x2="100" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="100" cy="123" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M93,123 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="80" y="123" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">230 V</text><line x1="266" y1="90" x2="304" y2="96" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="100" x2="304" y2="106" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="110" x2="304" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="120" x2="304" y2="126" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="130" x2="304" y2="136" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="140" x2="304" y2="146" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266" y1="150" x2="304" y2="156" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="90" x2="370" y2="90" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="304" y1="156" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="90" x2="370" y2="105" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="370" y1="141" x2="370" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="363" y="105" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="398" y="123" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">11.5 V</text><text x="165" y="222" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">primary: 0.10 A</text><text x="285" y="222" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">secondary</text></svg>', 'An ideal transformer drawing 0.10 A from a 230 V supply; the secondary gives 11.5 V across a load.'),
('db944d09-677f-5fbf-bed9-6a6f982c7a2d', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 12, 12, 'Why is electrical power transmitted at very high voltage?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The current is smaller for the same power, so less energy is wasted as heat in the cables', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P_loss = I²R, and I = P/V. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (The current is smaller for the same power, so less energy is wasted as heat in the cables).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('f84449a5-1dfe-5934-b394-2a0475d80b78', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 13, 13, 'A current of 50 A flows in a cable of resistance 4.0 Ω. Calculate the power wasted in the cable.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10000', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = I²R = 50² × 4.0 = 1.0 × 10⁴ W. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: P = I²R. A1: P = 1.0 × 10⁴ W.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('0eaca358-2e98-57e5-9067-a441963f5890', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 14, 14, 'How does an induction hob heat a metal pan?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'An alternating magnetic field induces eddy currents in the pan base, which heat it', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The changing flux induces currents in the conducting pan. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (An alternating magnetic field induces eddy currents in the pan base, which heat it).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('f001ab07-64c4-521f-8065-0661e578f9c7', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 15, 15, 'A generator coil of 200 turns and area 0.0050 m² rotates at 50 rad s⁻¹ in a field of 0.10 T. Calculate the peak e.m.f., using E₀ = NBAω.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E₀ = NBAω = 200 × 0.10 × 0.0050 × 50 = 5.0 V. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: E₀ = NBAω. A1: E₀ = 5.0 V.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('90da2284-7101-5ccd-bbae-20a0a3da0ad0', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 16, 16, 'A generator coil is turned faster. What happens to its output?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Both the peak e.m.f. and the frequency increase', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E₀ = NBAω and f = ω/2π. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (Both the peak e.m.f. and the frequency increase).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('162404df-8a78-5688-918b-ea8b09c74f47', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 17, 17, 'A simple a.c. generator turns at 3000 revolutions per minute. Calculate the frequency of its output.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '50', 'Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f = 3000 ÷ 60 = 50 Hz. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: revolutions per second. A1: f = 50 Hz.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('aef41224-8d3f-505e-9dac-9bc234869c23', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 18, 18, 'How does a wireless charging pad charge a phone?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'An alternating current in a coil in the pad induces an alternating e.m.f. in a coil in the phone', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The two coils act like the windings of a transformer. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (An alternating current in a coil in the pad induces an alternating e.m.f. in a coil in the phone).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('b549b77d-4ad8-55d9-b8d4-3f7eeef08e52', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 19, 19, 'A transformer takes in 120 W and delivers 114 W. Calculate its efficiency.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '95', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Efficiency = 114 ÷ 120 × 100 = 95 %. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: output ÷ input. A1: efficiency = 95%.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('cdac4a6e-1633-55d8-afcd-c2f95bfa4673', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 20, 20, 'How does an electric guitar pickup produce a signal?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The vibrating steel string changes the magnetic flux through a coil, inducing an e.m.f.', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The magnetised string moving near the coil gives a changing flux linkage. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (The vibrating steel string changes the magnetic flux through a coil, inducing an e.m.f.).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('fc19da5a-e383-54e5-8fff-64ffc25d16c9', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 21, 21, 'A transformer has three times as many turns on its secondary as on its primary. The primary voltage is 12 V. What is the secondary voltage?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '36', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Vₛ = Vₚ × Nₛ/Nₚ = 12 × 3 = 36 V. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: Vₛ = 36 V.', 1, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgde6ff5ce-t fgde6ff5ce-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgde6ff5ce-t">Step-up transformer</title><desc id="fgde6ff5ce-d">A transformer whose secondary has three times as many turns (3N) as its primary (N); the primary voltage is 12 V.</desc><path d="M150,46 a6,6 0 0,1 6,-6 h138 a6,6 0 0,1 6,6 v148 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,6 h-138 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,-6 Z M180,70 h90 v100 h-90 Z" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));fill-rule:evenodd;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="184" y2="96" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="100" x2="184" y2="106" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="110" x2="184" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="120" x2="184" y2="126" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="130" x2="184" y2="136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="140" x2="184" y2="146" style="stroke: