('8f26867e-4eb4-5b11-b071-870670bf4c3c', 'f7ead7fd-7729-4ec2-9a2e-7a00cfac7c96', '24d540aa-65ef-46d8-ac39-5c62ee4aed70', 'a-level', '26.5', '9702 coursebook 26.5 · Everyday examples of electromagnetic induction', 26, 26, 'Which change would increase the output voltage of a transformer?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Adding turns to the secondary coil', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Vₛ = VₚNₛ/Nₚ, so more secondary turns raise the output voltage. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Vₛ ∝ Nₛ. C1: other changes reduce or stop output. A1: C (Adding turns to the secondary coil).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg9f1366c1-t fg9f1366c1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg9f1366c1-t">Transformer</title><desc id="fg9f1366c1-d">A transformer: an a.c. supply across the primary coil and a load across the secondary coil, both wound on an iron core.</desc><path d="M150,46 a6,6 0 0,1 6,-6 h138 a6,6 0 0,1 6,6 v148 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,6 h-138 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,-6 Z M180,70 h90 v100 h-90 Z" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));fill-rule:evenodd;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="90" x2="184" y2="96" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="100" x2="184" y2="106" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="110" x2="184" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="120" x2="184" y2="126" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="146" y1="130" x2="184" y2="136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;s